then now I'm out in L.A.,

00:04:15.168 --> 00:04:17.867
and I've just recently
started dating again,

00:04:17.867 --> 00:04:18.780
so it's all right.

00:04:18.780 --> 00:04:20.120
- I love that, I love that.

00:04:20.120 --> 00:04:21.260
Carlton?

00:04:21.260 --> 00:04:22.093
- [Carlton] Yes?

00:04:22.093 --> 00:04:24.010
- So what's been going
on since the experiment?

00:04:24.010 --> 00:04:26.438
- I've really just been
working on Carlton.

00:04:26.438 --> 00:04:28.580
I'm single still.

00:04:28.580 --> 00:04:31.380
I've taken some self-reflection.

00:04:31.380 --> 00:04:34.928
Obviously what happened on
the show was major in my life.

00:04:34.928 --> 00:04:39.200
It was very important to me
to preserve my personal space

00:04:39.200 --> 00:04:43.040
and my mental space because
subject matters like that

00:04:43.040 --> 00:04:44.510
could take you down a dark road,

00:04:44.510 --> 00:04:46.600
so in the back of your
mind, you're thinking

00:04:46.600 --> 00:04:49.820
oh my God, did I really
just share my entire life?

00:04:49.820 --> 00:04:51.520
Like, there's no other secret.

00:04:51.520 --> 00:04:52.353
- Yeah.

00:04:52.353 --> 00:04:53.186
- [Carlton] You get what I'm saying?

00:04:53.186 --> 00:04:54.019
- Yeah.

00:04:54.019 --> 00:04:55.240
- So like, on one end I feel very free

00:04:55.240 --> 00:04:57.180
since doing the show but
then on the other end,

00:04:57.180 --> 00:04:59.680
I'm just very disappointed that, like,

00:04:59.680 --> 00:05:02.390
